through distribution comparison using Kullback-Leibler divergence across specific cities, and through cadaster datafrom Slovenia and Greece. The quality and completeness of the resulting dataset is similar to the cadaster datasets, revealingthat, while some misclassifications occur due to definitional differences or data limitations, the dataset overall provides reliableand valuable building information at global scale. Among other applications, one could reuse the data to identify vulnerabilitiesof buildings for natural hazards, to model population distributions based, or to calculate carbon footprints of buildings.\n\nThe data paper is accessible via [[https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-025-06132-z]].\nThe data publication is accessible via [[https://doi.org/10.5880/GFZ.LKUT.2025.002]].\n&quot;, &quot;limitBounds&quot;: {}, &quot;onLoadPanel&quot;: &quot;caption&quot;, &quot;shortCredit&quot;: &quot;Oostwegel et al. (2025)&quot;, &quot;zoomControl&quot;: true, &quot;permanentCredit&quot;: &quot;OpenBuildingMap \u00a9 [[https://www.gfz.de/|GFZ]]&quot;, &quot;fullscreenControl&quot;: true, &quot;displayPopupFooter&quot;: true, &quot;permanentCreditBackground&quot;: true, &quot;is_template&quot;: false, &quot;permissions&quot;: {&quot;edit_status&quot;: 2, &quot;share_status&quot;: 2, &quot;owner&quot;: {&quot;id&quot;: 10721, &quot;name&quot;: &quot;LaurensOostwegel&quot;, &quot;url&quot;: &quot;/de/user/LaurensOostwegel/&quot;}, &quot;editors&quot;: [], &quot;team&quot;: {&quot;id&quot;: 163, &quot;name&quot;: &quot;GFZ Section 2.6&quot;, &quot;url&quot;: &quot;/de/team/163/&quot;}}, &quot;author&quot;: {&quot;name&quot;: &quot;GFZ Section 2.6&quot;, &quot;url&quot;: &quot;/de/team/163/&quot;}, &quot;urls&quot;: {&quot;agnocomplete&quot;: &quot;/agnocomplete/AutocompleteUser/?q={q}&quot;, &quot;map_short_url&quot;: &quot;/m/{pk}/&quot;, &quot;ajax-proxy&quot;: &quot;/ajax-proxy/{ttl}/&quot;, &quot;password_change&quot;: &quot;/change-password/&quot;, &quot;password_cha